# Interview concepts with every part

When we start or explore a new portfolio part, create or update a matching interview-concepts doc in the same session. Do not wait until the part is finished.

- Path: `docs/interview-concepts-part-N.md` (example: `docs/interview-concepts-part-1.md`)
- If the part file already exists, add cards for any new concept we just used. Do not rewrite the whole file.
- Do not create a new part doc for a small follow-up on a concept already covered.

Match the Part 1 format:

- Title: `Interview Concepts: Part N`
- Intro: memorize as spoken answers; four prompts; do not claim later features
- Each concept: **Speak this**, then a table for What / Why / How I used it / How it can fail
- Optional **If they ask** follow-up
- End with a **30-second story** and a **Words to keep precise** table

Only document concepts that exist in the current part. If history, alarms, OPC UA, or .NET are not built yet, do not write cards that claim they are.

```markdown
# Interview Concepts: Part 2

Memorize these as spoken answers. Each card is **what it is**, **why this project needs it**, **how you used it**, and **how it can fail**. Do not claim OPC UA or .NET until those exist.

## 1. Tag history

**Speak this:**
One sentence an interviewer can hear first.

| Prompt | Answer |
|---|---|
| What is it? | ... |
| Why does this project need it? | ... |
| How did I use it? | ... |
| How can it fail? | ... |
```
